OL,3,GNEWSAHealth board admits failings that
OL,4,Aled to dementia patient's death
OL,5,
OL,6,FA health board has admitted safety
OL,7,Ffailings that led to the death of a
OL,8,Fhigh-risk dementia patient at a mental
OL,9,Fhealth facility in Perth.
OL,11,FAndrea Imrie, 82, died on 13 January
OL,12,F2024, a week after she fell and
OL,13,Fsustained catastrophic head injuries
OL,14,Fafter getting out of bed at Murray
OL,15,FRoyal Hospital.
OL,17,FPerth Sheriff Court heard an alarm had
OL,18,Fbeen removed from her bed the day
OL,19,Fbefore, and motion sensor alarms in her
OL,20,Froom failed to notify staff.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB  Scot NewsC Reg TVF  Weather
FL,426,420,260,160,0,100
